        Disk-integrated photometric data of asteroids do not contain accurate information on shape details or size scale. Additional data such as disk-resolved images or stellar occultation measurements further constrain asteroid shapes and allow size estimates. We aim to use all available disk-resolved images of about forty asteroids obtained by the Near-InfraRed Camera (Nirc2) mounted on the W.M. Keck I&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('1702.01996v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('1702.01996v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
